00:00:38.483 --> 00:00:39.780
Because there's one thing

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.347
that only a very few
people know in PowerPoint,

00:00:42.347 --> 00:00:45.740
and this is that, PowerPoint, by default,

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.680
messes up your text boxes.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.530
If you insert a new
text box in PowerPoint,

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:53.520
it will be messed up and
not be created in a way

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.110
that you actually wanted to be

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.970
and that's actually helpful
for you to work with it.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:59.810
This video will show you why

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:01.960
and it will show you how to fix that.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.400
So that by default, if
you insert new text boxes,

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.080
they will look exactly like you need them

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.100
and in a helpful and constructive way.

