00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.090
check it out and look at the link

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.700
to see more about it.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.800
So now I would like to show you something

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.860
that will really help you to improve

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.160
the way you make your
slides and your pages

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.390
and will really help
you to spend less time

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:03.530
to align all the elements on your page.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:05.150
It would be, I think, quite an improvement

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:06.420
of your workflow.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.750
The topic is fix your text boxes.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.740
The reason why I'm saying that is that

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.520
there's actually quite a problem

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:15.680
with the default text boxes in PowerPoint.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.440
Let me just show you one example

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.590
to really make it clear what I mean.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:20.650
Let's look at this page.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:22.810
This is just a random example page

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.660
that I prepared here for you.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.560
Now let's imagine this
text box wouldn't be there.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.090
So I delete it now.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:32.170
And we wanted to include
a new text box here.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.720
So what would I do usually?

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.430
I would here, click on 'text box,'

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:38.020
in order for me to insert a new text box.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:40.110
So click here to create a new one.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.450
Now I'll type in some kind of text,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.730
probably something like, I don't know.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.610
So this is the column potential offerings,

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:51.020
so 'create new casino offering,'

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.000
something like that.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.890
Obviously it doesn't make much sense now

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.900
but just as an example.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.720
Let's include a bullet here.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.270
Now you'll see the
formatting is a bit off.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:02.130
This is Calibri, the rest
of the page is in Ariel.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:07.070
So let's make this Ariel and
I think the font size was 14.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.067
So let's enter that as well.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.880
Now the text box should be exactly like

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.100
these other text boxes.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.550
Or is that maybe not the case?

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.100
What I want to show you
is now the following.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.660
Imagine how you want to
nicely fit this new text box

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.330
in the page and by doing
that we would like to

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.630
align it to this upper element here.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.380
And aligning means that
would really start here

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.300
at the left border of it.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.410
And you see all the other text boxes

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:37.290
with their bullet points,
they neatly start here

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:40.280
at the left edge of this element.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.110
And this gives it a nice and clean look.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.400
We will have the later section
on alignment of elements.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.540
But let's dive into it here at this point

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.280
and say we would like to
align it to this left edge.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.190
Probably the easiest way of doing that

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:56.047
would be to click here on 'arrange.'

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.667
'Align' and 'left.'

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.820
Now this is PowerPoint on a Mac.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.720
I usually always also
use the Windows version.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.620
The guide I think looks a bit different

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.780
but you will find this arrange pendant

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:13.303
somewhere in your Windows
PowerPoint as well.

00:04:14.425 --> 00:04:16.620
Now we aligned it here on the left, right?

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:20.013
It is supposed to start
here at the left corner.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.570
Now maybe let's.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:23.403
Whoops.

00:04:24.732 --> 00:04:26.743
Let's try to center this a bit.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:28.613
Like this.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:32.170
Actually we need to move it up

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:35.370
in order to make it symmetric together.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.560
Fine.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:39.770
What is now the problem that
we see with this element?

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:42.360
The problem is that if you look closely,

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.050
it isn't really starting at the left edge

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.083
of this thing.

00:04:47.564 --> 00:04:50.130
You will see it if you
mark all these objects,

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:54.260
that here the dot directly
starts at the edge of the border

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.220
of the box, but here it doesn't.

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:58.410
There is some kind of distance in between.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.530
And this is actually quite a problem

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.810
with the text boxes how they are created

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:05.330
as a default in PowerPoint.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.450
Because if you create a new text box,

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.500
it automatically inserts
a border to the left,

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.440
to the right, to the
top, and to the bottom.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:16.160
And this makes it really
hard to neatly align

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.870
the text boxes to each other.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:19.910
Because imagine now if all text boxes

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:21.670
would look like this text box.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.650
Just to demonstrate that to you

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.620
I will now copy this format and apply it

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:27.080
to the other boxes.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:30.610
If you don't know it, you can
use this format icon here.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:31.890
If you double click on it,

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.543
you can use it several times.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:38.350
If I now click here, it gets transformed

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.490
to the format of the reference object

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:44.650
that was marked or
highlighted in the beginning.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.830
Now, of course, the size is out of bounds

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:48.030
but that is not really the issue.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.963
We can just fix that.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:00.893
Like that.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.860
Now we've got to fix that as well

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:06.233
to where you can close it.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.160
If we focus now here on the left border,

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:10.993
what's the problem?

00:06:10.993 --> 00:06:12.540
The problem is that now

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.940
it isn't really neatly alignment here.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.060
The issue is that there's literally no way

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.510
for me to, with the
automatic alignment functions

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:24.770
that PowerPoints provide,
to make it neatly start

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:25.603
here at the end.

00:06:25.603 --> 00:06:29.770
Because if I use these autofitting guides,

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:33.210
it will just give me the guide
on the edge of the border

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:35.990
but not really the guide
where the point starts.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:39.570
So the only thing I can
do is manually try to

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:41.840
put it more or less
closely to where I think

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.200
the right position is,

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.330
which is obviously super cumbersome.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:48.270
And if you want to align
lots of objects on your page,

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:51.810
it would take ages and it's
just not a good work flow.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:53.660
Let's go back to where it was before.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:06:59.720
What you actually need to do

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.190
in order to fix this text
box is the following.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:06.240
You right click on it
and click 'format shape.'

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.373
Then some kind of menu will pop up.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.370
And here if you click on this icon here

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:15.080
and within the text box sub-menu,

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.960
you can 'resize shape to fit text'

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.310
and then, more important here,

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:20.840
the left margin, right margin,

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.790
top margin, and bottom margin.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.643
And you should put these all to zero.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.900
What you see now, now we've got this

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:32.620
kind of clean, neat, text box design.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:33.917
And if we move it somewhere else,

00:07:33.917 --> 00:07:37.897
and we want to realign it to
this reference header box,

00:07:37.897 --> 00:07:39.730
you just click align left.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.880
It neatly starts on the exact same level

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:43.120
where the others start.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.393
This is where it's supposed to be.

00:07:47.727 --> 00:07:49.280
Now the next thing you can do,

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:50.770
because obviously it's quite annoying

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:53.520
to have to fix every
single text box this way.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.530
There's one function
existing within PowerPoint

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.100
in order to make this text box style

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.810
the new default style.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:01.732
And if you right-click on the text box,

00:08:01.732 --> 00:08:03.935
on the border of the text box,

00:08:03.935 --> 00:08:08.355
you get this possibility to
'set as default text box.'

00:08:08.355 --> 00:08:10.685
If you click this, now PowerPoint knows

00:08:10.685 --> 00:08:12.860
that we want all text boxes to be created

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:14.043
exactly in this way.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.760
The next time that we
insert a new text box,

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:18.960
let's do that right now.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.173
I insert something,

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.120
I insert a random text in it,

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.960
and you're noticing that it
looks exactly the way it should.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.883
If we now align it to this text box,

00:08:35.752 --> 00:08:38.170
'align left,' it's neatly
aligned with all the other boxes.

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.250
And this is how we want it.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:42.870
So here's my really
important recommendation

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.700
that you set the text
boxes exactly in this way.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.560
You do not want to have any borders

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:51.010
around your elements that
are automatically inserted.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.410
Because otherwise the
whole alignment process

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:55.600
within PowerPoint will not work properly.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.140
It will just be a huge pain, huge pain,

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:01.770
to get neatly formatted
and neatly aligned pages.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.050
So do yourself this favor
and it will help you

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:05.990
throughout the rest of the course.

